| Feature        | Memoization  | Tabulation | Space Optimized |
| -------------- | ------------ | ---------- | --------------- |
| Approach       | Top-Down     | Bottom-Up  | Bottom-Up       |
| Uses Recursion | ✅ Yes        | ❌ No       | ❌ No            |
| DP Array       | ✅ Yes        | ✅ Yes      | ❌ No            |
| Stack Memory   | ✅ Yes        | ❌ No       | ❌ No            |
| Time           | O(n)         | O(n)       | O(n)            |
| Space          | O(n) + Stack | O(n)       | O(1)            |

Lekin generally fastest kaun hota hai?

Agar same problem ke sabhi states compute karni hain (jaise Fibonacci), to generally order hota hai:

🥇 Space Optimization (least memory, no recursion)

⬇️

🥈 Tabulation (no recursion)

⬇️

🥉 Memoization (recursion call overhead hota hai)

Recursion ke har function call ka overhead hota hai, 
isliye theoretical aur practical dono terms me Fibonacci 
ke liye memoization aam taur par tabulation aur especially 
space optimization se faster nahi hota.

To short answer:

Memoization: Top-Down approach, recursion use karta hai,
 sirf required states calculate karta hai.

Tabulation: Bottom-Up approach, recursion nahi hota, 
chhoti states se badi state build karta hai.

Space Optimization: Tabulation ka optimized version hai
jo unnecessary DP array hata kar sirf required previous values store karta hai.

Ye teenon Dynamic Programming ke important approaches hain aur problem ke hisab se inka use kiya jata hai.